					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: Jawn on December 21, 2006, 04:58:52 pm</div><div class="quote">The question remains, what will you guys do to prevent this?<br /></div><br /><br />The question is, what will you do? Not just you, Jawn, but everyone in Washington, especially the 20 and under crowd. Gotta take some responsibility, can&#039;t always wait for others to get the ball rolling.<br /><br />With that said, it&#039;d probably be a good first step to re-mobilize the forces that fought the Teen Dance Ordinance and identify a new generation of organizers to tackle this issue.</div>
					<br />
					<hr size="2" width="100%" />
					Title: <b>Re: THE END OF ALL AGES SHOWS?</b><br />
					Post by: <b>Jawn</b> on <b>December 21, 2006, 07:33:05 pm</b>
					<hr />
					<div style="margin: 0 5ex;"><div class="quoteheader">Quote from: olaf on December 21, 2006, 07:14:28 pm</div><div class="quote">The question is, what will you do? Not just you, Jawn, but everyone in Washington, especially the 20 and under crowd. Gotta take some responsibility, can&#039;t always wait for others to get the ball rolling.<br /><br />With that said, it&#039;d probably be a good first step to re-mobilize the forces that fought the Teen Dance Ordinance and identify a new generation of organizers to tackle this issue.<br /></div><br /><br />I emailed the Seattle Music Office and wrote a quick response to Mayor Nickels this afternoon. I&#039;ll do whatever else my community asks of me, but I just couldn&#039;t stand to see Sergio and Chris gasping &quot;fuck&quot; and &quot;shit&quot;, as if they didn&#039;t know what else to do. I don&#039;t mean to diss you guys, but I moved out to Seattle this summer to enjoy live local music, among other reasons. I&#039;d hate to see all my efforts wasted thanks to some assfucks who think they&#039;re doing us kids a favor.<br /><br />I hope everyone on this board acts soon. I really don&#039;t want the New Year&#039;s Eve party to end up my last concert until I turn 21, and I&#039;m sure the lot of you feel just as bored on saturday nights as well.</div>
